f retail, including grocery, mass, club, pet specialty, and international, as well as digital. The company was incorporated in 2004 and is headquartered in Bedminster, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William B. Cyr | CEO & Executive Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $913,652 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $856K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Defensive peers, with revenue growing 26%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $10K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Freshpet, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer defensive business with a $3.3B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +23% over the past three years and +25% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -4% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 44%.","The business throws off $12M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 5.4\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 400% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.000387687948078},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (19.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (83% sell ratio, net $23.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Consumer Defensive \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 10% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (FRPT) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/91/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_FRPT_Volatility_111126092601_1794407161.html","date":"2026-11-11","tim